<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bình Xuyên</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Binh Xuyen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bình Xuyên was an armed organisation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> in the 1940s and 1950s that grew from river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> and gangs into a private army under Bảy Viễn. It fought the French, then came to terms with them, and under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-vietnam">State of Vietnam</a> controlled the Saigon police, gambling and prostitution. The army of Ngô Đình Diệm defeated it in street fighting in 1955.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/binh-xuyen.jpg" alt="Bình Xuyên" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cikki · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Binh_Xuyen_Army.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
